    <div class="article-intro"><div class="article-hero"><img src="/assets/blog/recarga-condominio.webp" width="1280" height="720" alt="Residents check shared EV charger rules and booking schedule" fetchpriority="high"></div><header class="article-header"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal"></span>VeVolt guide</p><h1>Shared EV charger in a condominium: rules, booking and usage</h1><p class="lede">A shared charger works best when every resident sees the same availability and understands booking duration, tolerance, session records and bay-release rules.</p><p class="article-meta">Updated 03/08/2026 · 1 min read</p></header></div>
    <div class="article-layout"><div class="article-body"><section><h2>Define access and responsibilities</h2><p>Identify authorized users, approved vehicles and who handles incidents. App membership does not replace physical access controls for the equipment or parking area.</p></section><section><h2>Build a workable booking policy</h2><p>Set booking length, cancellation notice, tolerance and maintenance blocks. Connect each completed booking to a manual session record so monthly review has context.</p><ul><li>Booking duration</li><li>Cancellation notice</li><li>Late-arrival tolerance</li><li>Maintenance blocks</li><li>Session completion</li></ul></section><section><h2>Review conflicts and adjust</h2><p>Track disputed time slots and repeated overruns. VeVolt does not physically block the charger outside a reservation; consistent rules remain essential.</p></section><nav class="article-context-links" aria-label="Continue the condominium charging guide"><h2>Continue the condominium charging guide</h2><ul><li><a href="/en/condo">Manage bookings with VeVolt Condo</a></li><li><a href="/en/blog/electric-car-charger-in-condominium">Read the pillar guide</a></li><li><a href="/en/blog/allocate-ev-charging-costs-condominium">Plan manual cost allocation</a></li></ul></nav><section><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><div class="faq-list"><details class="faq-item"><summary>Can VeVolt lock a charger outside a booking?</summary><p>No. It organizes the schedule without controlling hardware.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How many chargers can a hub include?</summary><p>Up to 10 private chargers.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Can residents see available times?</summary><p>Yes. Invited participants use the shared schedule to avoid overlapping reservations.</p></details></div></section></div>
    <aside class="article-aside"><h2>Organize with VeVolt Condo</h2><p>Organize residents, schedules, sessions and manual cost allocation with VeVolt Condo. Eligible new customers can try the monthly plan free for 15 days on Google Play.</p><a class="play-badge-link" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=br.com.vevolt" rel="noopener" aria-label="Get it on Google Play"><img src="/assets/google-play-badge-en.png" width="564" height="168" alt="Get it on Google Play"></a><h2>Sources and further reading</h2><ul class="source-list"><li><a href="https://www.agenciasp.sp.gov.br/governo-de-sp-sanciona-lei-que-permite-instalacao-de-carregadores-de-carros-eletricos-em-condominios/" rel="noopener noreferrer">São Paulo State Government - Charging in condominiums</a></li><li><a href="https://www.ba.gov.br/ssp/noticias/2026-05/88443/cbm-homologa-instrucao-tecnica-para-seguranca-em-recarga-de-veiculos" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bahia Fire Department - Safety at EV charging locations</a></li></ul></aside></div>
